---
import Section from './Section.astro';
// Personal science — a pattern from your own data, tested hard enough to rule out
// coincidence. The statistical method names are gone (owner); the card keeps its
// product chrome and the plain "not a fluke" framing.
---

<Section id="personal" labelledby="personal-h">
  <h2 id="personal-h" class="rise mt-4 max-w-2xl text-[clamp(1.9rem,4vw,3rem)]">
    Patterns from <span class="text-accent-soft">your</span> days — not a study’s.
  </h2>

  <div class="mt-10 grid items-center gap-12 lg:grid-cols-[1fr_1fr] lg:gap-16">
    <div class="rise">
      <p class="lede">
        It watches for connections in your own history, then tests each one hard enough to rule out
        coincidence — so a “finding” is a real signal, not just something that caught your eye on a chart.
      </p>
      <p class="mt-5 text-[0.95rem] leading-relaxed text-ink-faint">
        Most apps don’t bother. And a pattern in your own days is the strongest nudge there is —
        because it’s yours, not an average borrowed from strangers.
      </p>
    </div>

    <figure
      class="surface surface-lift surface-key rise p-6 sm:p-7"
      aria-label="Rendered example: a personal finding about late caffeine, tested to rule out coincidence"
    >
      <figcaption class="flex items-center justify-between gap-3">
        <span class="mono text-[0.66rem] uppercase tracking-[0.16em] text-ink-faint">
          A pattern in your data
        </span>
        <span class="chip chip-warn chip-dot">from your data</span>
      </figcaption>
      <hr class="hairline my-5" />
      <p class="display-line text-[1.55rem]">
        Coffee after <span class="mono">~3&thinsp;pm</span>
        <span class="text-ink-faint">&rarr;</span>
        <span class="text-accent-soft">&minus;40 min</span> sleep
      </p>
      <p class="mt-4 text-[0.92rem] leading-relaxed text-ink-soft">
        On the nights you logged a late coffee, you slept about 40 minutes less. Measured against your
        own normal — your pattern, not an average pinned onto you.
      </p>
      <dl class="mono mt-5 grid grid-cols-[auto_1fr] gap-x-4 gap-y-1.5 text-xs text-ink-faint">
        <dt>compared</dt><dd class="text-ink-soft">late-coffee nights vs the rest</dd>
        <dt>over</dt><dd class="text-ink-soft">your last 60 days</dd>
        <dt>verdict</dt><dd class="text-ink-soft">real, not a fluke</dd>
      </dl>
    </figure>
  </div>
</Section>
